# flow-harness — provider configuration template. COPY to `.env` and fill in real
# keys. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed as documentation. `docker compose`
# auto-loads `.env`; for a local `node` run: `set -a; source .env; set +a`.
#
# Every tier (haiku / sonnet / opus) resolves independently from FLOW_LLM_<TIER>_*,
# falling back to the blanket FLOW_LLM_* vars, and finally to the offline FakeProvider
# (so tests and dry runs need no key). See packages/llm/src/config.ts.

# ── Primary providers per tier ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# CEO / judgment tier (opus) — a strong model. Anthropic, or any OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint (Gemini shown). provider ∈ { anthropic | openai | fake }.
# FLOW_LLM_OPUS_PROVIDER=openai
# FLOW_LLM_OPUS_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# FLOW_LLM_OPUS_API_KEY=
# FLOW_LLM_OPUS_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro

# Execution tiers (sonnet/haiku) — a cheap/fast model. Groq shown.
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_PROVIDER=openai
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_API_KEY=
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# ── Automatic fallback per tier ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# If a tier's primary complete() throws (saturation / outage, after retries), the
# ModelRouter auto-switches to this backup. Use it for overflow when many jobs run
# in parallel. OpenRouter is OpenAI-compatible (provider=openai); its :free models
# are slow but make a fine extra pair of hands. Browse https://openrouter.ai/models.
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=openai
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_FALLBACK_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-REPLACE_ME
# FLOW_LLM_SONNET_FALLBACK_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324:free
# FLOW_LLM_HAIKU_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=openai
# FLOW_LLM_HAIKU_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# FLOW_LLM_HAIKU_FALLBACK_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-REPLACE_ME
# FLOW_LLM_HAIKU_FALLBACK_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324:free
